1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:03,611
SOULHABIT: This bottle says eleven percent. Does
that mean eleven percent ectoin?

2
00:00:03,951 --> 00:00:07,277
SOULHABIT: No. It's a blend. Which is
why the most useful thing you

3
00:00:07,296 --> 00:00:10,642
can do with an ectoin product
is turn the bottle around.

4
00:00:10,942 --> 00:00:14,187
SOULHABIT: But before skincare marketing
found it, ectoin belonged

5
00:00:14,207 --> 00:00:17,471
to a bacterium living
in extremely salty water.

6
00:00:17,751 --> 00:00:20,749
JAY: Bacteria invented skincare?

7
00:00:21,029 --> 00:00:23,244
SOULHABIT: Not intentionally.

8
00:00:23,584 --> 00:00:27,098
SOULHABIT: The salt is constantly trying
to pull water out

9
00:00:27,118 --> 00:00:30,632
of the cell, basically turning
it into a microscopic

10
00:00:30,652 --> 00:00:34,186
raisin. Ectoin helps keep the
delicate machinery inside stable.

11
00:00:34,526 --> 00:00:38,925
SOULHABIT: Skincare borrowed the molecule.
Marketing borrowed the drama.

12
00:00:39,225 --> 00:00:42,213
SOULHABIT: Ectoin belongs to a group of

13
00:00:42,233 --> 00:00:45,241
protective molecules sometimes called extremolytes.

14
00:00:45,581 --> 00:00:49,950
SOULHABIT: Its proposed effects involve how water
arranges itself around proteins and

15
00:00:49,971 --> 00:00:54,360
membranes. One part of the
explanation is called preferential exclusion.

16
00:00:54,640 --> 00:00:58,845
JAY: Even the alarm wants
you to stop.

17
00:00:59,185 --> 00:01:03,008
SOULHABIT: Fine. Imagine a protein is
a celebrity surrounded by security.

18
00:01:03,288 --> 00:01:06,294
SOULHABIT: Ectoin may help the
surrounding water remain organised

19
00:01:06,314 --> 00:01:09,340
without simply clinging directly
to the protein.

20
00:01:09,680 --> 00:01:12,252
JAY: So ectoin gives

21
00:01:12,272 --> 00:01:14,864
proteins personal space.

22
00:01:15,144 --> 00:01:18,455
SOULHABIT: That is the simplified explanation. The

23
00:01:18,475 --> 00:01:21,806
actual molecular behaviour is more complicated.

24
00:01:22,146 --> 00:01:25,079
JAY: Understood. Ectoin is a hydration

25
00:01:25,099 --> 00:01:28,051
event coordinator with excellent boundaries.

26
00:01:28,331 --> 00:01:32,137
SOULHABIT: I immediately regret simplifying this.

27
00:01:32,437 --> 00:01:36,743
SOULHABIT: Laboratory research suggests ectoin may help
stabilise biological structures and influence

28
00:01:36,763 --> 00:01:41,090
how keratin in the outer
skin layer interacts with water.

29
00:01:41,430 --> 00:01:44,691
SOULHABIT: It may help dry or
stressed skin cope more comfortably.

30
00:01:44,971 --> 00:01:47,348
JAY: Look at you translating yourself.

31
00:01:47,628 --> 00:01:48,822
SOULHABIT: I am learning.

32
00:01:49,162 --> 00:01:52,486
JAY: Does ectoin create an invisible protective

33
00:01:52,506 --> 00:01:55,850
force field around my face?

34
00:01:56,130 --> 00:01:58,090
SOULHABIT: No.

35
00:01:58,370 --> 00:02:01,136
JAY: Finally, a skincare ingredient

36
00:02:01,156 --> 00:02:03,941
with realistic boundaries.

37
00:02:04,281 --> 00:02:08,258
SOULHABIT: Think of ectoin as support for
the skin barrier, not body armour.

38
00:02:08,558 --> 00:02:12,151
SOULHABIT: In one study, 104 women
compared a cream containing

39
00:02:12,171 --> 00:02:15,785
2 percent ectoin with the
same cream without it.

40
00:02:16,065 --> 00:02:18,453
SOULHABIT: The women preferred the ectoin version.

41
00:02:18,753 --> 00:02:21,347
JAY: So it worked?

42
00:02:21,627 --> 00:02:25,140
SOULHABIT: They liked it better. That is
a real result, but it is

43
00:02:25,160 --> 00:02:28,693
not the same as a machine
proving that their skin transformed.

44
00:02:28,973 --> 00:02:32,016
JAY: Preference, not Cinderella.

45
00:02:32,316 --> 00:02:36,044
SOULHABIT: Another study followed 65 people
with mild to moderate eczema.

46
00:02:36,064 --> 00:02:39,793
Over four weeks, the ectoin
cream performed about as well

47
00:02:39,813 --> 00:02:43,561
as the comparison barrier cream
and was well tolerated.

48
00:02:43,861 --> 00:02:45,336
JAY: Promising?

49
00:02:45,616 --> 00:02:46,716
SOULHABIT: Yes.

50
00:02:46,736 --> 00:02:48,158
JAY: Miracle?

51
00:02:48,438 --> 00:02:49,538
SOULHABIT: No.

52
00:02:49,558 --> 00:02:53,071
SOULHABIT: It does not prove
that ectoin cures

53
00:02:53,091 --> 00:02:56,625
eczema, reverses ageing or
replaces medical treatment.

54
00:02:56,905 --> 00:03:00,716
SOULHABIT: The clinical evidence is still
limited, and some research

55
00:03:00,736 --> 00:03:04,567
is connected to companies
that sell the ingredient.

56
00:03:04,867 --> 00:03:07,015
JAY: How limited?

57
00:03:07,295 --> 00:03:10,448
SOULHABIT: A PubMed search found
twelve clinical trials.

58
00:03:10,728 --> 00:03:13,791
JAY: Twelve? My group chat
has produced more research

59
00:03:13,811 --> 00:03:16,893
on whether someone should
text their ex.

60
00:03:17,173 --> 00:03:19,092
SOULHABIT: None of it passed peer review.

61
00:03:19,392 --> 00:03:23,008
SOULHABIT: Ectoin may be most interesting
if your skin is

62
00:03:23,029 --> 00:03:26,665
dry, sensitive, over-cleansed or irritated
by a demanding routine.

63
00:03:26,945 --> 00:03:29,756
SOULHABIT: It can be paired
with ingredients such

64
00:03:29,776 --> 00:03:32,608
as panthenol, glycerin, squalane and ceramides.

65
00:03:32,948 --> 00:03:36,012
SOULHABIT: Exactly. Check the actual percentage
when it is disclosed,

66
00:03:36,032 --> 00:03:39,117
read the ingredient list and
judge the complete formula.

67
00:03:39,397 --> 00:03:42,330
JAY: One fashionable ingredient cannot rescue

68
00:03:42,350 --> 00:03:45,303
a badly built product.

69
00:03:45,583 --> 00:03:48,203
SOULHABIT: You may deactivate the
Jargon Alarm now.

70
00:03:48,503 --> 00:03:52,123
SOULHABIT: K-beauty did not invent ectoin.

71
00:03:52,143 --> 00:03:55,783
Bacteria developed the survival strategy.

72
00:03:56,063 --> 00:03:59,783
SOULHABIT: Korean formulators are using
it alongside familiar barrier-supporting

73
00:03:59,803 --> 00:04:03,544
ingredients in lightweight serums,
toners and sun products.

74
00:04:03,824 --> 00:04:06,769
JAY: So bacteria invented it, and

75
00:04:06,789 --> 00:04:09,754
Korea gave it better packaging.

76
00:04:10,034 --> 00:04:12,755
SOULHABIT: Aggressively simplified, but acceptable.

77
00:04:13,055 --> 00:04:17,506
SOULHABIT: Ectoin is not the new hyaluronic
acid. It is not a

78
00:04:17,526 --> 00:04:21,997
miracle, and the evidence is not
strong enough for dramatic promises.

79
00:04:22,297 --> 00:04:26,092
SOULHABIT: It is a genuinely
interesting supporting ingredient

80
00:04:26,112 --> 00:04:29,926
that may help dry
or stressed skin.

81
00:04:30,206 --> 00:04:33,661
JAY: Supporting actor, not superhero.

82
00:04:33,961 --> 00:04:38,468
SOULHABIT: Exactly. Look for the actual percentage,
then judge the whole formula.

83
00:04:38,768 --> 00:04:43,094
JAY: And would I put a bacteria-made
survival molecule on my face?

84
00:04:43,374 --> 00:04:44,474
SOULHABIT: Would you?

85
00:04:44,617 --> 00:04:47,696
JAY: I have already purchased snail mucus.

86
00:04:47,716 --> 00:04:50,814
The dignity ship sailed years ago.

87
00:04:51,094 --> 00:04:52,519
SOULHABIT: Fair enough.

88
00:04:52,819 --> 00:04:56,824
JAY: What questionable skincare ingredient
are we investigating next?
